formulas.interpretation:
Using the Clifford anticommutation relation, one verifies that $[\Sigma^{\mu
u}, \Sigma^{ho\sigma}] = i(\eta^{
uho}\Sigma^{\mu\sigma} - \eta^{\muho}\Sigma^{
u\sigma} - \eta^{
u\sigma}\Sigma^{\muho} + \eta^{\mu\sigma}\Sigma^{
uho})$, matching the Lorentz algebra exactly. In four-dimensional Minkowski spacetime, the spatial components $\Sigma^{ij} =  rac{1}{2}\epsilon^{ijk}\operatorname{diag}(\sigma_k, \sigma_k)$ generate spatial spin rotations with eigenvalues $\pm  rac{1}{2}$, whereas $\Sigma^{0i}$ generate non-unitary Lorentz boosts.
